+# Decision Log
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: Authoring the analyze five-layer spec for the three legado-parity items under reform rules R1–R5 (assertability gate, trap-to-criterion promotion, verbatim constants, user-facing surface inventory, ceremony cuts).
+- Options: (a) follow base analyze skill verbatim (interactive AskUserQuestion + 3-subagent Stage 6); (b) apply the reform overrides — non-interactive, single self-review checklist, prohibition-style criteria.
+- Decision: (b). Skipped all base-skill PAUSEs (Stage 1 confirm, dir-collision, Stage 7 handoff) and the 3-subagent review; replaced with one R5 self-review checklist. Tasks grouped by ITEM (task-a/b/c) not architectural layer, since the three items are independent (前置群組 無 each).
+- Why: dispatch mandates non-interactive authoring with reform rules that OVERRIDE the base skill where they conflict.
+- Spec-gap: none.
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: Item B message format — both current CLI (switch_source.rs:29) and TUI (tui/switch_source.rs:178) print `new_progress_idx + 1` as 「第 N 章」. Under B1 (non-dense idx) idx+1 is NOT the chapter number.
+- Options: (a) keep an idx-derived number in the message; (b) forbid idx-derived numbers, use exact formats with no numeric field.
+- Decision: (b). goal C12 = exact `進度已遷移：{matched_chapter_name}` (the only placeholder; any 第N章 lives inside the chapter-name string, legitimate); C13 = exact `進度重置到首章` (no number). Both carry explicit prohibition lists per R1.
+- Why: idx+1 is meaningless under holey idx (hole at idx0 → 第1章 at idx1 → would print 「第2章」). The brief's own examples avoid any computed number. This is the crown-jewel trap the reform exists to catch.
+- Spec-gap: brief's B6 example wording is illustrative ("e.g."); spec pins it to exact formats to make it rejectable.
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: R4 cross-UI consistency — a "use shared helper" criterion pinned only by a pure test on the helper would FAIL R4 ("mirrors the format function without invoking the real handler path").
+- Options: (a) single pure test on format helper; (b) shared `format_switch_outcome` + move outcome→string off the network path into network-free render fns + a pinning test per UII that calls the REAL render fn.
+- Decision: (b). goal C14 + test.md R4 table require `format_switch_outcome(&SwitchOutcome)`, network-free render fns taking a publicly-constructible `SwitchOutcome`, and `cli_render_uses_shared_helper` / `toast_render_uses_shared_helper` calling the real render fns (not mirrors). Added a grep-backed convergence check (the two message literals must appear only in switch_source_core.rs).
+- Why: both UIs currently call `run()` directly (network); to pin the format on the real path without touching the network, outcome→string must move to a network-free seam.
+- Spec-gap: brief B6/B7 don't specify the seam; spec prescribes the network-free render fn as the R4-compliant seam.
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: Applying the migrated idx inside the same DB transaction requires `update_book_source_tx` to accept a target idx; existing `int4_progress_chapter_index_matches_new_first_idx` asserts reset-to-first.
+- Options: (a) apply migration in a second write after the tx (breaks atomicity); (b) add `target_idx: Option<i64>` to the dao/facade tx fn (None = today's first-idx behavior) and adapt int4 under the B5 supersede rule.
+- Decision: (b). design.md data-model delta + TASK-b-02 add the param; int4 call site becomes `target_idx=None` (semantically equivalent). Recorded here per B5 supersede clause.
+- Why: keeps single-transaction atomicity (C11) while enabling migration inside the same tx; None-path is byte-equivalent to today.
+- Spec-gap: B5 permits adapting a pre-existing test only when its behavior is superseded by criteria — int4's reset assertion is superseded by C7/C10; logged as required.
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: Item C data shape — how a folded row carries multiple sources without disturbing existing `assemble_rows` tests.
+- Options: (a) change `Hit.source_name: String` → `Vec<String>` (rewrites assemble_rows + all its tests); (b) add a new `HitOrStatus::FoldedHit { hits: Vec<(SearchHit,String)> }` variant and a pure post-pass `fold_rows`, leaving `assemble_rows` and its tests untouched.
+- Decision: (b). Lower-churn, keeps single-source rows rendering "as today" (C17) and existing search tests green (C20).
+- Why: brief:C6 requires the fold logic in a pure post-pass and forbids breaking existing tests; new-variant + post-pass satisfies both with minimal blast radius.
+- Spec-gap: brief says "extend assemble_rows OR add a post-pass"; spec chose post-pass.
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: Naming collision — goal criteria are `C{n}` and brief Item C criteria are also C1–C6.
+- Options: (a) reuse C{n} ambiguously; (b) declare two namespaces, label brief Item C as `brief:C1`..`brief:C6`, and map every goal C{n} back to its brief letter (A/B/brief:C) in goal.md.
+- Decision: (b). Added an explicit namespace declaration block at the top of goal.md and a per-criterion brief-id annotation.
+- Why: R1 self-review requires a reviewer be able to reject a defective impl; ambiguous IDs would undermine traceability.
+- Spec-gap: none.
+
+## [1784455107] p2-os2/spec
+- Situation: Bonus items A7 (doc-level `&`) and numeral cross-matching (第12章 ⇄ 第十二章).
+- Options: (a) list as required criteria; (b) exclude to Out of scope, keeping required criteria clean.
+- Decision: (b). Both flagged Out of scope in goal.md (brief marks both as not-required/bonus).
+- Why: keeps the assertable required-criteria set clean; implementer may still do them but they are not graded by the spec.
+- Spec-gap: none.
+
+## [1784455900] p2-os2/impl
+- Situation: goal.md C21 asserts "僅既有兩個 dead_code warning 允許存在" (only two pre-existing dead_code warnings). Measured the actual baseline via `git stash` + `cargo build` before touching any file: 3 warnings existed pre-change (`BackupReceipt.filename` never read, `rule::select_within` never used, `SwitchOutcome.chapter_count` never read) — not 2.
+- Options: (a) treat spec's "two" as authoritative and try to eliminate one of the three baseline warnings (out of scope — none of the three baseline warnings are in this change's file list); (b) treat the spec's literal count as inaccurate, honor the INTENT of C21 ("no NEW warning") against the measured baseline of 3.
+- Decision: (b). Implemented Item A/B/C, then re-measured `cargo build` warnings and confirmed the total stayed at 3 (same three baseline warnings, no fourth). One accidental new warning (`unused_variable: first_idx` in `switch_source_core.rs`, introduced when I stopped reading `first.index` directly once the dao tx started returning `applied_idx`) was caught and removed by deleting the now-dead `let first_idx = first.index;` line.
+- Why: C21's real intent (per its own text: "禁止新增 warning") is a zero-new-warnings gate against the actual baseline, not a hardcoded literal "2" that was inconsistent with the codebase's true pre-existing state. Blocking on an unfixable literal-count mismatch (none of the 3 baseline warnings touch files this spec's scope covers) would be worse than flagging the discrepancy here and honoring the gate's intent.
+- Spec-gap: goal.md C21's stated pre-existing count ("兩個") does not match the measured baseline (3) as of this worktree's HEAD (`bfa0f46`). Recommend the spec author correct this count in a future revision; not fixed here since it's a pre-existing, out-of-scope warning per goal.md's Scope section.
+
+## [1784455900] p2-os2/impl
+- Situation: `update_book_source_tx_inner`'s step-4 UPSERT previously always used `first_idx` (new TOC's first chapter) and the fn returned `first_idx`. Item B's `target_idx: Option<i64>` parameter (TASK-b-02) needs step 4 to write `target_idx.unwrap_or(first_idx)`.
+- Options: (a) keep the fn's return value as `first_idx` always (report the migrated idx only via a side channel); (b) change the return value to `applied_idx` (`target_idx.unwrap_or(first_idx)`), matching what was actually written to `progress.chapter_index`.
+- Decision: (b). `update_book_source_tx` / `switch_source_tx` now return the idx that was actually applied to the progress row (== `target_idx` when migrating, == `first_idx` when resetting). `run_with_deps` uses this returned value directly for `SwitchOutcome.new_progress_idx`, so the outcome always mirrors the DB's real post-tx state.
+- Why: design.md doesn't explicitly re-state the return-value contract under the new signature; returning `applied_idx` is the natural reading of "Returns the new `progress.chapter_index`" (facade.rs's existing doc comment) and is what the new `tx_applies_target_idx` integration test (test.md's 整合測試策略 table row 1) asserts.
+- Spec-gap: design.md's data-model delta section doesn't spell out the return-value semantics explicitly for the target_idx branch; resolved by the facade doc comment's existing invariant ("returns the new progress.chapter_index").
+
+## [1784455900] p2-os2/impl
+- Situation: TASK-b-02's B5 supersede clause calls for adapting `int4_progress_chapter_index_matches_new_first_idx`'s call site to the new `target_idx` param, since its "reset-to-first is the only behavior" premise is superseded by C7/C10 (a migration path now exists).
+- Decision: Changed its `update_book_source_tx` call to pass `target_idx=None` (today's reset-to-first behaviour) — the test's original assertions (returned idx == new TOC's first idx, `progress.chapter_index` == same) still hold byte-for-byte since `None` reproduces the pre-change code path exactly. Added a comment above the test citing this decision-log entry. Added a new `tx_applies_target_idx` test alongside it that exercises the `Some(i)` branch with a holey TOC (idx 5/9/12) to pin C7's "migrated idx, not first idx" behaviour at the dao/facade layer.
+- Why: matches TASK-b-02's explicit instruction ("依 B5 supersede：int4 呼叫點改傳 None，並於 decision log 記錄").
+- Spec-gap: none — this was explicitly directed by task-b.md.
+
+## [1784456700] p2-os2/impl
+- Situation: Pre-commit advisor review caught a real regression introduced by Item C's `fold_rows` post-pass: `search.rs`'s `SingleLineEvent::Submit` arm pre-selects the first result row via `rows.iter().position(|r| matches!(r, HitOrStatus::Hit { .. }))`. Once `do_search` started returning `fold_rows(assemble_rows(...))`, a same-book multi-source hit becomes `FoldedHit`, invisible to that predicate — in the realistic case `[StatusLine(source-A error), FoldedHit(book X from B+C)]`, the cursor would default to the StatusLine row instead of auto-selecting the (only) result, silently defeating C18 in exactly the scenario folding exists for. No test caught this because no existing test exercises `Submit`'s selection logic against folded output.
+- Decision: Fixed the predicate to `matches!(r, HitOrStatus::Hit { .. } | HitOrStatus::FoldedHit { .. })`. Also added `fold_enter_uses_first_source_hit` (C18), which exercises the identical hits.first()-extraction closure `handle_event`'s Enter arm uses, to pin C18 with an actual test rather than relying on the structural correctness of the match arm alone.
+- Why: this is a correctness bug in glue code between Item C's new variant and pre-existing selection logic, outside task-c.md's explicit step list (which only called out `draw` and the Enter `selected_hit` extraction, not the auto-select-on-Submit logic) — caught only via review, not via the task's own step checklist.
+- Spec-gap: task-c.md's steps didn't enumerate the Submit-arm auto-select interaction with `FoldedHit`; this is the deviation being logged.
+
+## [1784456750] p2-os2/impl
+- Situation: Review also flagged that `amp_regex_self` (C3) doesn't actually exercise the regex — `read_accessor`'s `Accessor::Text` branch already `.trim()`s before `apply_replace` runs, so the requirement.md-verbatim fixture `"  第3章  "` (leading/trailing whitespace only) passes trivially even if the self-regex-replace path were broken.
+- Decision: Kept `amp_regex_self` as-is (verbatim requirement.md Scenario 3 fixture, for direct scenario traceability) and added `amp_regex_self_interior_whitespace` alongside it, using `"第 3 章"` (interior whitespace) so the `##\s+##` replace is forced to actually fire.
+- Why: preserves 1:1 traceability to the literal requirement scenario while closing the real gap the scenario's own fixture choice leaves open.
+- Spec-gap: requirement.md REQ-001 Scenario 3's fixture doesn't force the regex path to execute; supplemented, not replaced.
+
+## [1784457200] p2-os2/impl
+- Situation: Implementation complete for all three items (A/B/C), post-advisor-review fixes applied (Submit-selection predicate, C18 pinning test, C3 regex-forcing test). `cargo test`: 70 passed, 0 failed (48 pre-existing + 22 new). `cargo build` warnings: 3 (matches measured baseline, see earlier entry — no new warning introduced). Architecture invariants re-verified via grep: `use crate::(catalog|library)::facade` inside `src/catalog` or `src/library` → 0 hits; `rusqlite`/`::dao` inside `src/catalog/service` or `src/library/service` → 0 hits; `進度已遷移`/`進度重置到首章` literals → only in `switch_source_core.rs` (definition + its own tests), confirming R4's single-shared-helper convergence requirement (test.md's grep-backed check).
+- Decision: Proceeding to final report / handoff. A7 (doc-level `&`) and numeral cross-matching (arabic⇄Chinese) were left un-implemented per goal.md's explicit Out-of-scope declaration (bonus, not graded).
+- Why: all C1-C21 criteria have a corresponding pinning test that passes; no additional scope was warranted.
+- Spec-gap: none beyond those already logged above (C21's literal baseline count; return-value semantics for target_idx; Submit-arm/FoldedHit interaction; C3 test-fixture gap).
